description:
FILED s514d (Opus, 2026-10-10) while measuring #2590 on t/op/tiehandle.t (its `package Bar::Say; use base qw(Implement)` block aborts: rows 37-44 of the file never run).

A `package X;` switch inside a bare BLOCK that also holds a `local` is lowered by the nested-switch path (Parser2 _lower_block_1, the #3120 site), which emits at RUN TIME `(p-defclass X::plc-x () ())` -- a class with NO parents.  p-defclass compares parents, so it REDEFINES the class that `use base` had already given its parents: perl's `package X;` never changes @ISA.  The `use base` push also emits an unqualified `(p-push @ISA ...)` inside the block.

Minimal reproducer (perl 5.40.3 prints `hi [Implement] []`; PCL dies "Can't locate object method "hi" via package "Bar""):

    package Implement; sub hi { "hi" }
    package main;
    { package Bar; use base qw(Implement); local $\ = ""; print Bar->hi, " [@Bar::ISA] [@main::ISA]\n"; }

Without the `local` the same block works (it takes the section path).  Fix direction: a run-time package switch ensures the class EXISTS and never sets its parents (e.g. a p-defclass form that creates when absent and leaves an existing class alone); probe the `@ISA` push's package too.  Costs t/op/tiehandle.t rows 37-44.

=== DONE (s514f, Opus, commit 7123a6a9 on the s515 rebase) ===
Two halves, both in the task.  (1) The nested-switch path (Parser2 _lower_block_1) emits the NEW exported macro p-ensure-class (create the class when absent; an existing class is left exactly as it is) instead of a parentless p-defclass -- a run-time `package X;` never sets parents (ir-spec).  (2) `use base` / `use parent` after such a switch emitted a bare `@ISA` (and a bare class name) READ in the enclosing section's package, so main got the parents and X none: Parser::_process_use_base now qualifies the class + @ISA through ONE predicate _reader_pkg_differs, shared with the `use` :into target (rule 11; the condition was inline at that site).  Guard Pl/t/defclass-01.t +3 (rows 15-16 fail on base 8f2fa11c; row 17 = the no-local control).  ACCEPTANCE: t/op/tiehandle.t alone 53/1 (+13 never produced) -> 66/1; the one red row is 57 (`use warnings; print undef` expects an uninitialized-value warning PRINTed through the tied STDERR -- warnings-gated diagnostics are absent, #221).  Baselines edited row by row (perl-suite-run.tsv, perl-suite-fails.tsv 16 rows -> 1, row-shortfall.tsv row removed).  Fable's pkgblock.pl == perl.
